18:16:00 said  Built **Minecraft Jukebox** as a native Rust desktop app: a pixel-styled shelf of all 18 discs, a central jukebox with insert/eject animations and floating notes, plus eject, volume, seek, repeat, previous/next controls and keyboard shortcuts. It plays the disc files already installed with Minecraft, asks for your Minecraft folder on first launch, remembers it, and bundles no copyrighted music.
18:16:00 said  I verified a clean release build, all five tests, a scripted run that switches discs, inserts one and checks the on-screen controls, and a 120-frame window screenshot; it found all 18 discs in the Minecraft folder on this Mac. The artwork is original procedural pixel art rather than Minecraft’s real textures, and the animation timings are documented estimates because there was no reference build. Next, open it, pick your folder, and tell me which disc or visual detail you’d like polished.
