20:01:21 out   ---MECH---
20:01:21 out   # Minecraft Jukebox - mechanics sheet
20:01:21 out   This is a player, not a combat game, so the "mechanics" are the timing,
20:01:21 out   navigation, layout and playback rules that make the jukebox feel like the
20:01:21 out   Minecraft block. There is no reference build in this workspace, so every value
20:01:21 out   that the request did not specify is marked **estimated**. The request values are
20:01:21 out   marked **request**.
20:01:21 out   ## Discs and inventory
20:01:21 out   | Setting | Value | Source |
20:01:21 out   |---|---|---|
20:01:21 out   | Music discs in the catalogue | 22 | request follow-up |
20:01:21 out   | Discs, in display order: 13, cat, blocks, chirp, far, mall, mellohi, stal, strad, ward, 11, Creator (Music Box), wait, Creator, Precipice, Otherside, Relic, 5, Pigstep, Tears, Lava Chicken, Bounce | exact list | request follow-up |
20:01:21 out   | Grid columns at the default window width | 11 (two rows of 22 discs) | estimated |
20:01:21 out   | Grid columns at medium width | 9 (three rows) | estimated |
20:01:21 out   | Grid columns at narrower widths | 6 / 5 / 4 | estimated |
20:01:21 out   | Disc card width | computed from available width, 80 px minimum | estimated |
20:01:21 out   | Disc artwork size in a card | 38-64 px, nearest-neighbour | estimated |
20:01:21 out   | Selected disc highlight | 2 px gold border + gold title | estimated |
20:01:21 out   | Missing track marker | 4 px red square + "MISSING" | estimated |
20:01:21 out   The four discs added in the follow-up use the composers shown on the Minecraft
20:01:21 out   Wiki's Music Disc page: Creator (Music Box) - Lena Raine, Tears - Amos Roddy,
20:01:21 out   Lava Chicken - Hyper Potions, Bounce - fingerspit. Their colours are original
20:01:21 out   procedural pixel-art palettes, not the game's textures.
